<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common User Adoption Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Organizations may experience low user adoption when customers
                    struggle to understand the product or do not see enough value
                    in changing their existing workflows. Identifying adoption
                    barriers helps teams create more effective improvement strategies.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Complex User Experience:</b> Complicated navigation, unclear
                    interfaces, and unnecessary steps can discourage users from
                    adopting important product capabilities.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Poor Onboarding:</b> Users may abandon a product when they are
                    not clearly guided through the initial setup or do not understand
                    how to achieve their first meaningful outcome.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Lack of Awareness:</b> Users may not know that certain features
                    exist or understand how those features can help them. Product
                    education and contextual guidance can improve feature discovery.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Insufficient Training:</b> Complex products may require structured
                    training and documentation. Providing appropriate learning resources
                    can increase confidence and product usage.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Resistance to Change:</b> Users may prefer existing processes
                    and hesitate to adopt new workflows. Demonstrating clear benefits
                    and providing transition support can improve adoption.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Feedback:</b> Without continuous user feedback, teams
                    may not recognize adoption problems quickly. Regular feedback
                    helps identify and resolve barriers.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant adoption challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

